	array(
		'question_text'  => 'A therapist concludes that a client’s spiritual experiences are symptoms of a psychotic disorder. The therapist has not asked what the experiences mean to the client, assessed whether they are accepted within the client’s community, evaluated distress or impairment, or considered alternative explanations. When the client objects, the therapist becomes defensive.What is the most appropriate response?',
